{:id "0004-conversation-core"
 :title "Conversation core: the app's state and actions, handled purely"
 :lupa/deps #{"0001-perform"}
 :lupa/area :core
 :lupa/risk :high
 :goal "The browser app's whole behaviour as a pure function: (handle state
        action) -> {:state :effects}. It holds one conversation, its members,
        messages, and presence; the composer; which messages are performing
        and since when; and the reader's preferences. Views and the shell
        built later only render state and run effects."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/app/core.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/core_test.cljc"]
 :design "New namespace halfahead.app.core (.cljc, no interop). Public:

          initial-state      ; a map; :prefs {:reduced-motion? false :sound? false}
          (handle state action) -> {:state s :effects [[:fx/... & args] ...]}
          (frames state)     -> {message-id frame} for every message, in the
                                shape of halfahead.perform/frame-at

          State keys (plain map, document them in the ns docstring):
          :me (member id), :conversation, :members {id member}, :messages
          {id message}, :presence {member-id presence}, :composer {:text s},
          :now-ms n, :performing {message-id started-at-ms}, :prefs.

          Actions are vectors; everything time- or id-dependent travels in
          the action:
          [:session/started {:me id :conversation c :members [m ...]
                             :now-ms n :reduced-motion? b}]
          [:messages/received {:messages [msg ...] :initial? b :now-ms n}]
            merge by :id. When :initial? is false, each message not seen
            before starts performing at :now-ms. Initial history never
            performs: it arrives settled.
          [:presence/received {:presence [p ...]}]
          [:composer/edited {:text s}]
          [:composer/sent {:id id :now inst}]
            when the trimmed text is non-blank: emits
            [:fx/write-message msg] with a valid :ha/message (author :me,
            delivery :plain, emphasis [], sent-at :now) and clears the
            composer; otherwise does nothing (no effect, state unchanged).
          [:clock/ticked {:now-ms n}]
            updates :now-ms and drops finished performances (now past
            started + the timeline's :duration-ms).
          [:message/skipped {:id id}] settles that message at once.
          [:prefs/changed {:reduced-motion? b :sound? b}] (either key)
          [:replay/requested {:id id :now-ms n}] performs that message again.
          Unknown actions return the state unchanged with no effects.

          frames: for a performing message, frame-at of its timeline at
          (- now-ms started-at); for any other message, its final frame. The
          timeline comes from halfahead.perform/perform with the message's
          text, delivery and emphasis, :reduced-motion? from :prefs, and a
          seed derived deterministically from the message id (e.g. a string
          hash computed the same on JVM and JS — implement it, do not use
          clojure.core/hash, which differs between hosts).

          Also public: (awaiting-agent? state) -> true when the latest
          message is from a human and some agent member's presence is
          :thinking (the view shows a thinking line)."
 :acceptance
 ["Every action listed has a test asserting the resulting state and effects"
  "composer/sent with text \"  hi \" emits exactly one :fx/write-message whose
   message is a valid :ha/message with text \"hi\", and clears the composer;
   with blank text it returns state unchanged and no effects"
  "messages/received with :initial? true performs nothing; with :initial?
   false a new message is in :performing at :now-ms, and a message already
   present is not restarted"
  "clock/ticked past a performance's duration removes it; frames then give
   that message's final frame (all progress 1.0)"
  "With :reduced-motion? true, a newly received message's frame at its
   arrival time already shows all text at progress 1.0"
  "Property: for any sequence of the listed actions, every message's frame
   concatenates to exactly its text (flair never alters content)"
  "The seed function gives the same number for the same id across calls and
   is defined without clojure.core/hash"
  "Unknown action -> same state, no effects"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit halfahead.schema, halfahead.perform, bb.edn, or the test runner"
  "No views, DOM, Firebase, timers, or clock reads; no routing; one
   conversation only"]
 :context ["DESIGN.md" "docs/SCHEMA.md" "src/halfahead/schema.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/perform.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 10.0}
